{"prompt": {"messages": [{"role": "system", "content": "You are a helpful assistant that translates C++ code to Java 8 code. The code should reads and writes I/O from the console."}, {"role": "user", "content": "Translate the following GNU C++ code to Java 8 code. The code reads and writes I/O from the console. Your translated code should have the exact same functionality as the given code, meaning that it should have the same output for any given input.\nPrint your translated code and also the confidence score you give to your translation. The confidence score should be a number between 0 and 1. The format of the output should be:\n<translated_code>\n<your_translated_code>\n</translated_code>\n<confidence>\n<your_confidence_score>\n</confidence>\nDo not provide any other text or markdown fences.\n\nHere is the original GNU C++ code you have to translate:\n<original_code>\n#include<iostream>\n#include<cstdio>\n#include<cstdlib>\n#include<cstring>\n#include<algorithm>\n#include<cmath>\n#include<queue>\n#include<set>\n#include<stack>\n#include<map>\n#include<vector>\n#include<bitset>\n#define fi first\n#define se second\n#define pb push_back\n#define mk make_pair\nusing namespace std;\ntypedef long long ll;\ntypedef unsigned long long ull;\nll read()\n{\n    char ch=getchar();ll x=0,f=1;\n    while(ch<'0'||ch>'9')\n    {\n        if(ch=='-') f=-1;\n        ch=getchar();\n    }\n    x=ch-'0';\n    while(1)\n    {\n        ch=getchar();\n        if(ch<'0'||ch>'9') break;\n        x=x*10+ch-'0';\n    }\n    return x*f;\n}\nconst ll mod=1e9+7;\nll p,k,ret;\nll qmul(ll a,ll b,ll Mod)\n{\n    ll ans=0;\n    while(b)\n    {\n        if(b&1) ans=(ans+a)%Mod;\n        b>>=1;a=(a+a)%Mod;\n    }\n    return ans;\n}\nll qpow(ll a,ll b,ll Mod)\n{\n    ll ans=1;\n    while(b)\n    {\n        if(b&1) ans=qmul(ans,a,Mod);\n        b>>=1;a=qmul(a,a,Mod);\n    }\n    return ans;\n}\nint main()\n{\n  //  freopen(\"B.in\",\"r\",stdin);\n   // freopen(\"B.out\",\"w\",stdout);\n    p=read(),k=read();\n    if(k==0) ret=qpow(p,p-1,mod);\n    if(k==1) ret=qpow(p,p,mod);\n    if(k>1)\n    {\n        ll l=1,cur=k;\n        while(cur!=1)\n        {\n            cur=(ll) cur*k%p;\n            l++;\n        }\n        ret=qpow(p,(p-1)/l,mod);\n    }\n    printf(\"%I64d\\n\",ret);\n  //  fclose(stdin);\n  //  fclose(stdout);\n    return 0;\n}\n           \n</original_code>\n"}], "temp": 0, "sample_size": 1, "logprobs": true, "model": "deepseek/deepseek-v4-flash"}, "response": {"samples": [{"content": "<translated_code>\nimport java.util.Scanner;\n\npublic class Main {\n    static final long MOD = 1000000007L;\n\n    static long qmul(long a, long b, long mod) {\n        long ans = 0;\n        while (b > 0) {\n            if ((b & 1) == 1) {\n                ans = (ans + a) % mod;\n            }\n            b >>= 1;\n            a = (a + a) % mod;\n        }\n        return ans;\n    }\n\n    static long qpow(long a, long b, long mod) {\n        long ans = 1;\n        while (b > 0) {\n            if ((b & 1) == 1) {\n                ans = qmul(ans, a, mod);\n            }\n            b >>= 1;\n            a = qmul(a, a, mod);\n        }\n        return ans;\n    }\n\n    public static void main(String[] args) {\n        Scanner sc = new Scanner(System.in);\n        long p = sc.nextLong();\n        long k = sc.nextLong();\n\n        long ret;\n        if (k == 0) {\n            ret = qpow(p, p - 1, MOD);\n        } else if (k == 1) {\n            ret = qpow(p, p, MOD);\n        } else {\n            long l = 1;\n            long cur = k;\n            while (cur != 1) {\n                cur = (cur * k) % p;\n                l++;\n            }\n            ret = qpow(p, (p - 1) / l, MOD);\n        }\n        System.out.println(ret);\n    }\n}\n</translated_code>\n<confidence>\n1.0\n</confidence>", "token_logprobs": [-4.768370445162873e-07, 0.0, -4.768370445162873e-07, -9.476689592702314e-05, -9.298280929215252e-06, 0.0, -5.686121585313231e-05, -0.59774190187454